.TH SDL_PushGPUFragmentUniformData 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PushGPUFragmentUniformData \- Pushes data to a fragment uniform slot on the command buffer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_PushGPUFragmentUniformData(
.BI "    SDL_GPUCommandBuffer *command_buffer,
.BI "    Uint32 slot_index,
.BI "    const void *data,
.BI "    Uint32 length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Subsequent draw calls in this command buffer will use this uniform data\[char46]
.PP
The data being pushed must respect std140 layout conventions\[char46] In practical terms this means you must ensure that vec3 and vec4 fields are 16-byte aligned\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I command_buffer
a command buffer\[char46]
.TP
.I slot_index
the fragment uniform slot to push data to\[char46]
.TP
.I data
client data to write\[char46]
.TP
.I length
the length of the data to write\[char46]
.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

